      "point": "The abstraction of ATP hydrolysis as a bar-splitting event to introduce flexibility lacks a rigorous thermodynamic connection to the free energy of chemical bond cleavage. Without explicitly linking the assigned rate constants to the chemical potential of ATP, it is unclear how the model accounts for the driving force required to maintain non-equilibrium cycling in a physical system.",
      "topic": "Thermodynamic grounding"
    },
